  "body": "Closes #8036 — design #835 phase 3, the session half (phases 1–2 landed in #4535 and #8034: the journal gate and the actor-authorized operations). A joined session can now act on its live capability instead of the admin secret.\n\n## What changed\n\n**Joined builder install** (`install_begin` in a joined session)\n- `admin_token` is now optional on the frame. A joined `install_begin` that omits it installs on the session capability's authority; one that carries it is refused as mixed credentials before any scope check. The pre-join admin path is unchanged, except a missing token there is now refused explicitly (\"module install denied\") instead of failing the admin comparison.\n- New `WorldService::install_wasm_authorized`: early `BUILDER` check before any upload bytes are received, then the admin path's exact safeguards (the chunk loop is now a shared `receive_module_upload`), the publisher trust gate, module-directory save, blob pin — and the actor's own re-check at the effect boundary in `install_program_authorized`, which derives the `BuilderInstalled { by }` audit actor from the capability. No session-supplied value names the actor.\n- Builder installs are **Wasm-only**: a native artifact gets `InvalidModule` even on hosts with native execution enabled, so builder authority can never reach the native installer.\n\n**Joined moderator revoke** (new `revoke` client frame)\n- Carries only `participant_id`; handled via `revoke_authorized` (phase 2), so the journal's `Revoked { by }` is actor-derived. Success — and the no-op inactive-target case (`revoked: false`, no journal record) — replies with the new `revoked` server frame. The victim's session is closed by the existing revocation broadcast.\n\n**Stable denial code**\n- `ServerFrame::Error` gains an optional `code`, omitted for every existing error (serialized shape unchanged). Joined role denials use exactly `actor_denied` — one non-oracular code for invalid, expired, revoked, and insufficient capabilities, mirroring the CapError code from the capability layer.\n- New `WorldCommand::AuthorizeScope` / `WorldHandle::authorize` lets session paths classify a denial before doing work (before receiving upload bytes; before attempting a revoke). The operation commands still re-check inside the actor, so a capability revoked mid-upload is refused at the boundary — covered by a test that revokes the builder after `upload_ready` and asserts no activation and no `BuilderInstalled` journal entry.\n\n**Shell contract revision 6** — `install_begin` phases add `joined` and `admin_token` becomes `string?`; `revoke` (admin class, joined) and `revoked` (reply) frames named; `error` gains `code: string?`. The CLI contract-check expectation moves to v1.6 with it.\n\n## Tests\n\nEight new SessionIo tests in `world_session::tests`: builder install + journal attribution + program live; guest install denied `actor_denied` with session surviving; mixed credentials; mid-upload revocation; native upload refused; pre-join token omission; moderator revoke + victim disconnect + journal attribution + no-op re-revoke; guest revoke denied.\n\n- `cargo test --lib -- world_session:: shell_contract::` — 79 passed\n- `cargo test --lib -- world::` — 274 passed\n- `cargo test --test world_roles` — 7 passed\n\nWorked by the repo-health queue worker (lane code-g, task 14374) from the phase-3 scope in #8036 and design `doc/2026-11-01_design_id835.md` §5.\n\n---\n🤖 agent-note:v1 — queue task 14374 (lane code-g). Phase 3 of design #835; phases 1–2 already merged (#4535, #8034).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796959738&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=8494&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F8494&signature=fbc240f29dbd38f000954cf59dd41d7551ed94c9ae814eb654c1bf3f546b11ae\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/8494?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
